who is one of dancehall
and reggae's most prolific

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.190
and successful musicians ever.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.800
His latest single is called "Dem Time Deh"

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.600
featuring Manuel Turizo.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.430
Listen now wherever you get your music,

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.350
everybody say hello to Sean Paul.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:24.350
(audience cheering)
(upbeat music)

00:00:42.496 --> 00:00:44.670
Hello, hello. I like all your bling.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.195
- Thank you.
- Yes.

00:00:46.195 --> 00:00:47.028
- Crazy stuff.
- You're like,

00:00:47.028 --> 00:00:47.861
"I work hard for this."

00:00:47.861 --> 00:00:49.260
(Sean laughs)
Y'all met, right?

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:50.100
You know each other?

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.000
- Yeah, yeah, just now.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:51.833
- Oh, okay.
- Yeah, I was

00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:53.213
on "Saturday Night Live" a while back.

00:00:53.213 --> 00:00:54.660
- Oh, okay, okay.
- I don't know

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.130
if you were there that day, but-

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.200
- I was there that day, but we
didn't get a chance to meet.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.373
We don't get a chance to meet every-

00:00:59.373 --> 00:01:00.206
- I know.
- Single time.

00:01:00.206 --> 00:01:01.950
But yeah, no, I've been a
big fan for a long time.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:03.120
- Salute, man. Same, same.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.940
- So wait, your stage
name is Sean da Paul.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:06.930
What is that from?

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:08.823
- Sean Paul is my name.

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:11.820
My name is Sean-Paul.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:16.200
But there's a famous
cricketer in the Caribbean,

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.810
and his name is Chanderpaul,
that's his last name.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:20.370
And it sounded so much like my own.

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:21.203
Yeah, there he is.

00:01:21.203 --> 00:01:23.040
- Yeah.
- And he's from Guyana.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:26.040
And a lot of people came at me

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:27.960
because I first said he's from Trinidad,

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.600
and I made a mistake, excuse me.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.870
But, you know, it was a friend
of mine who was freestyling,

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:38.730
and I was going next on the
mic, like, doing freestyling.

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:41.040
And he was like, "Yo, Sean da Paul."

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.337
And everybody laughed and they were like,

00:01:42.337 --> 00:01:44.340
"Yo, that's the cricketer's name."

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:47.100
But it kind of stuck on me as
a nickname around the studio.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.620
And I started to say it in songs and-

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:50.970
- I love that.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:51.960
- Yeah (laughs).

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.430
- I found this incredible too.

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:56.160
So you grew up around
a lot of country music.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.147
- Jamaica, we love all
kind of different music.

00:01:59.147 --> 00:02:00.123
- Yeah.
- You know?

00:02:00.123 --> 00:02:02.520
And so, yeah, we have a lot of people

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.530
who are fans of country music.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:06.120
I think it reminds us of reggae.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:10.080
It tells a story. It's that type of music.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.020
So yeah, Kenny Rogers and Willie Nelson.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.599
- Kenny Rogers.
- I love Willie Nelson, man.

00:02:14.599 --> 00:02:15.432
- I love this.
(audience applauding)

00:02:15.432 --> 00:02:17.760
- I knew Willie Nelson
was coming up there.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:18.593
- Willie Nelson-
(Sean da Paul laughs)

00:02:18.593 --> 00:02:20.100
- I needed to check.
- Was coming in there. Yeah.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.120
- He's a Jamaican.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:21.953
- Yeah, but he-
- I think he's Jamaican.

00:02:21.953 --> 00:02:22.884
- He's a lifestyle.

00:02:22.884 --> 00:02:24.270
(Sean chuckles)
Yeah (chuckles).

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:26.222
- He's honorary Jamaican.

00:02:26.222 --> 00:02:27.870
- That's right. Yeah.
(audience laughs)

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.540
- Or we're honorary
listeners to his music.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:31.380
- Right. Brilliant.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.430
- But yeah-
- On top of it,

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:33.263
he smokes a lot of weed.

00:02:33.263 --> 00:02:34.950
- Yeah.
- Yeah (laughs).

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:36.924
- I went on his bus once and I was like...

00:02:36.924 --> 00:02:37.830
♪ Hey ♪

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:40.284
And then I walked off a different human.

00:02:40.284 --> 00:02:41.490
(Sean chuckles)
(Kelly chuckles)

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:43.410
- We have similar, you know,

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:44.460
what we call-
- Loves and interests?

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:45.600
- Interests.
- Yes.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.760
Yeah. Love languages if you will.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:48.593
Yes.
- For sure.

00:02:48.593 --> 00:02:51.360
- So wait, so your new single
is called "Dem Time Deh."

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:52.193
- You got it right.
- That's the music? Okay.

00:02:52.193 --> 00:02:53.026
"Dem Time Deh."
- Yes, you're right.

00:02:53.026 --> 00:02:54.600
- Yeah. What does that mean?

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.550
- It means back in the day. Dem time deh.

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:57.870
Those times there.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:01.920
So basically, a lot of people
kind of remember my career

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.870
from about 20 years ago,

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:07.350
and Manuel, he's a lot younger than me.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:10.410
And he was like, "Yo, back
in those days was awesome,

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.330
and I wanna do a song like that with you."

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.190
And he came to the studio
and he started writing,

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:15.900
and he's like, "What do
you want to call it?"

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:20.520
And I said, "Since it's so
reminiscent of dem time deh,

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.410
let's call it "Dem Time Deh," he loved it.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.240
I've been trying to bridge the gap

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:28.020
between reggaeton and dancehall
music or reggae music,

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.490
because we're such close in proximity

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:36.270
to Puerto Rico and
Dominican Republic, Cuba,

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:37.800
but we don't speak the language.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.560
And so, we do speak music though.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:42.830
- Yeah, connection, man.
Music is magical like that.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:44.790
- For sure.
- I love when you go to a show

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:45.720
and you look around,

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.220
that's my favorite part
of getting on stage.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:48.427
And I look at the audience and I'm like,

00:03:48.427 --> 00:03:50.700
"Where would all of us
be in the same room?"

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.140
You know what I'm saying?
Other than this moment.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.400
You just happen to like these songs,

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.810
you happen to like this vibe.

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:55.890
I love that about music.

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:57.930
That never gets old.
- Music gets us together.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:00.390
It gets us through some crazy times.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:03.510
My mom was telling me a story
about one of your songs,

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:04.343
and she was like,

00:04:04.343 --> 00:04:07.410
she was doing some very
mundane stuff one day,

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:09.690
sweeping floors and that kind of stuff.

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:11.340
And a lot of people was helping her out,

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:13.530
and she started singing
"A Moment Like This."

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:14.460
- Are you serious?

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:16.170
- Yeah, 'cause it was kind of funny,

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:18.030
'cause nobody wants to wait-

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:19.827
- A moment. Yeah.
- Their whole life to do that.

00:04:19.827 --> 00:04:21.093
Right?
(audience laughing)

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:22.732
- Your mom is funny.
(Sean chuckling)

00:04:22.732 --> 00:04:24.600
- So she said, "I must big you up,"

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.670
and it helped everybody get through it.

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:29.656
They all was singing it
and motivated them to-

00:04:29.656 --> 00:04:30.489
- Well, she has-
- Finish the job

00:04:30.489 --> 00:04:31.555
they were doing.
- Incredible taste, Sean.

00:04:31.555 --> 00:04:32.808
- (laughs) Yeah, she does.
(audience laughing)

00:04:32.808 --> 00:04:33.641
- That's right.
- Yes.

00:04:33.641 --> 00:04:34.541
- She does.
- She has incredible taste.

00:04:34.541 --> 00:04:35.424
(Kelly laughs)
- Thank you.

00:04:35.424 --> 00:04:38.287
- All right, we've got a
performance of the new single,

00:04:38.287 --> 00:04:41.520
"Dem Time Deh," from Sean
Paul featuring Manuel Turizo

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:42.570
coming up later.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:45.543
You can download the song now
wherever you get your music.

